{
  "version": "5",
  "_comment": [
    "Shared conformance vectors for the Claudia calendar write gate.",
    "",
    "Claudia writes to this calendar from TWO codebases: the Python paths in",
    "control_centre.live_gcal, and the forked Node calendar MCP the agent calls.",
    "Both must enforce the SAME rules, or an event can reach the calendar",
    "through whichever one is laxer -- and the lax one would be the Node side,",
    "which is where the school-document events (and D3) come from.",
    "",
    "This file is the contract. Both test suites load it and assert identical",
    "outcomes. Canonical copy lives in the Claudia repo at",
    "phase-shared/calendar_envelope/gate-vectors.json; the fork gets a deployed",
    "copy at src/handlers/core/gate-vectors.json.",
    "",
    "DRIFT TRIPWIRE: both implementations hardcode the expected `version`. To",
    "change these vectors you must bump `version` here AND the constant in",
    "calendar_envelope/envelope.py AND the constant in calendarEnvelope.ts --",
    "so a one-sided edit fails both suites instead of silently diverging."
  ],
