  "_idempotency_comment": [
    "v3 — D1. These matter MORE than the validation vectors, because a",
    "mismatch here is silent and expensive: if Python and TypeScript slug a",
    "title differently they derive DIFFERENT ids for the same event, both",
    "inserts succeed, and the duplicate the whole phase exists to prevent",
    "comes straight back — with no error anywhere to notice it by.",
    "",
    "The expected event_ids are pinned literally. They are frozen by caution 4:",
    "changing the derivation orphans every event the pipeline has ever written,",
    "so a change here is a migration with an explicit old->new mapping pass, not",
    "an edit. If one of these values ever needs to move, that is the signal to",
    "stop and write the migration."
  ],
