  "_preserve_comment": [
    "v5 - preserve_stored_envelope: what an UPDATE may and may not overwrite.",
    "ensure_envelope is fill-if-absent against the OUTGOING body. An update body is",
    "built from scratch, so every field the caller did not mention is 'absent', gets",
    "the pessimistic default, and the PATCH writes it over the row's real value.",
    "Found 2026-09-19 on live rows: the first two vectors are those rows.",
    "Each case: `body` (after ensure_envelope) + `stored` (the row as read) ->",
    "`private`, the body's private properties after the call. Exact equality.",
    "Rules: a GENERIC source ('control_centre', 'calendar-mcp', empty) never replaces",
    "a stored source; the default policy 'unclassified' never replaces a stored",
    "classification while the location is unchanged (whitespace/case-insensitive);",
    "any other policy in the body is a claim and wins; a moved event keeps its",
    "truthful 'unclassified'; nothing is ever deleted."
  ],
